  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The probability of a hit on a single shot is \\(1/2\\). The complement of at least 1 hit is misses on all 3 shots. What is the probability of at least 1 hit in 3 independent shots?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "7/8",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Each shot misses with probability \\(1-\\frac12=\\frac12\\). Since the shots are independent, the probability of missing all three is\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac12\\right)^3=\\frac18.\n\\]\nAt least one hit is the complementary event, so its probability is \\(1−1/8=7/8\\).",
